# Original IA32 cooperative-thread encodings, authored directly as Zero data.
# Extend the existing IA32 bank after its baseline table; no foreign compiler,
# assembler, linker or assembly source is involved.
# Native values use EDX:EAX. Every context slot is u64 with a zero high half.
# Context80: PC0,SP8,BP16,cursor24,arg0=32,arg1=40,flags48,result56,
# arenaBase64,version72. Version1. Child result1; parent/suspended result0.
# Child stacks: base16-aligned, size>=81920, private64KiB arena,64 locals,
# copied pending expression stack, and at least1024 bytes below childSP.
# Locals are copied by value. Existing pointers remain shared; future reserve
# allocations use the new child's empty arena.
# Fork rejects wrapping/high pointers, ctx8/base16 misalignment and overlap
# with its80-byte context, source locals/header, and source live operands.
# Its48-byte helper scratch is also protected. Switch protects32-byte scratch,
# rejects overlapping context records, and validates target frame geometry.
# Register temporaries are volatile at Zero statement boundaries. Saved flags
# are restored directly; these operations contain no CLI or STI.
# Prologue53: record immutable arenaBase at EBP+12 as well as cursor at EBP+8.
!store64[@templates + 0 | "8b4424048b54240883e4f083ec108904248954240489e581ec0002000089e731c0b980000000fcf3ab81ec0000010089650889650c"].
!store64[@templates + 8 | 53].
